[History]
___ with a history of HTN, CKD, BPH status post two prostate surgeries (most recent TURP was ___, multiple urological procedures since childhood, and recurrent UTI, who initially presented to ___ with fevers, malaise, and left scrotal swelling status post operative I&D of scrotum on ___, subsequently found to be in complete heart block, transferred to ___ for temporary pacing wire placement.   Patient presented to ___ on ___ with ___ days of scrotal swelling, malaise, and subjective fevers. Reported gradually increasing left sided scrotal swelling with overlying redness, which was non-tender, and not associated with any urological symptoms. Straight caths ___ times a day at baseline; did not notice any changes in consistency or smell of urine. Did not measure his temperature, but subjectively felt warm. Denied other infectious symptoms including abdominal pain, diarrhea/constipation, shortness of breath, cough, or nasal congestion. No recent sexual intercourse.  At ___, he was noted to have an elevated WBC of 16.2, and urine studies were notable for positive nitrites, ___ RBCs, ___ WBCs, 3+ bacteria, and 2+ epithelial cells. Patient was started on IV Zosyn for possible epididymitis and UTI and  urology were consulted. Unfortunately no subsequent records were sent with the patient and BID Community ___ was not working for the patient upon arrival. Per transfer email; "Patient went into the OR today (___) for an I&D of the left scrotal abscess and was found to be in complete heart block after the procedure." Transferred to ___ for temporary PPM.  On further questioning, patient reports checking his pulse on a regular basis when he is at home. Over the past few weeks he has noticed his pulse has been much slower, over half the rate it usually is, reporting it has been in the ___ on occasions.  Denies worsening fatigue, shortness of breath, light-headedness, dizziness, pre-syncope, or syncope. In fact, patient reports walking one mile about one week ago without any issues.   Upon arrival to ___, patient was taken immediately to the  cath, where a RIJ temporary pacing wire was inserted without complication, with appropriate capturing documented post same.   Post procedure, patient denies any symptoms. Understands he may need a permanent pacemaker in the future once source control for his GU infection has been established.  10-point review of systems otherwise notable for chronic fatigue   Past Medical History: - BPH status post two prostate surgeries (last TURP ___ - Multiple urological procedures since childhood - CKD (baseline 1.4-1.6) - HTN  - Recurrent UTI - Vertigo    Social History: ___ Family History: Grandfather with history of lung cancer and pacemaker placement. Brother with multiple urological procedures since childhood. Otherwise no other significant family history.

[Physical examination]
